#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst 37c5fa299da64046bfbe1fac5606da7c
msgid "OMA_get_hog tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:61 8cc8052fa23c49e2a6dcf1fbd4c4df83
msgid "**Name**: ``OMA_get_hog``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:63 51dab113ec64412e96eb0df91c857101
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get Hierarchical Orthologous Group (HOG) information "
"from OMA. HOGs represent groups of genes that descended from a single "
"ancestral gene within a given taxonomic range. HOGs capture the full "
"evolutionary history of gene families including gene duplications. "
"Example: HOG:E0739094 returns the p53 HOG at the Euteleostomi level with "
"description 'cellular tumor antigen p53', completeness score 0.65, and "
"child HOGs for fish, mammals, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:67 8b5c5e1b4e954cfb8d36d83929f7ba56
msgid ""
"``hog_id`` (string) (required) Hierarchical Orthologous Group ID. "
"Examples: 'HOG:E0739094' (p53 family), 'HOG:E0817124' (insulin family). "
"Use OMA\\_get\\_protein to find the HOG ID for a specific protein."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:84 b59dafb629504c938b3cfd1763c2012a
msgid "**OMA_get_orthologs** (Type: OMATool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:86 2da96458d28b4e54b28602aa9c134055
msgid ""
"Get pairwise orthologs for a protein from the OMA (Orthologous MAtrix) "
"Browser. Returns orthologo..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst 2ef1a68e4415436b88cc8658ca04f766
msgid "OMA_get_orthologs tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:92 2c6f770e404b4b398e155c7b3178966b
msgid "**Name**: ``OMA_get_orthologs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:94 38e8db965af34b4bb0921922412a969b
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get pairwise orthologs for a protein from the OMA "
"(Orthologous MAtrix) Browser. Returns orthologous proteins across species"
" with relationship type (1:1, 1:many, many:1, many:many), evolutionary "
"distance, and alignment score. OMA orthologs are inferred using a "
"rigorous algorithm that provides high-confidence predictions. Example: "
"P04637 (human p53) returns orthologs in 200+ species including Mus "
"musculus, Danio rerio, and Drosophila melanogaster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:98 7bbd737b1e5e4c718e37c745ed3f562a
msgid ""
"``protein_id`` (string) (required) UniProt accession (e.g., 'P04637' for "
"human p53) or OMA ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:101 322159572c49401ebdcfb3612c11244b
msgid ""
"``rel_type`` (string, null) (optional) Filter by orthology relationship "
"type. Options: '1:1' (one-to-one), '1:n' (one-to-many), 'n:1' (many-to-"
"one), 'n:m' (many-to-many). Leave empty for all types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:104 0792da5e181d491b9f1beed395bee3c7
msgid ""
"``per_page`` (integer, null) (optional) Number of orthologs to return "
"(default: 20, max: 100)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:121 ca3e48371a364da3a6dbc680df007a7c
msgid "**OMA_get_protein** (Type: OMATool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:123 23edb8ee6d3e47d2a8c98b23649cc01f
msgid ""
"Get protein information from the OMA (Orthologous MAtrix) Browser by "
"UniProt accession or OMA ID...."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst 3c35c0e067bd4cc88b7ce9da65660d26
msgid "OMA_get_protein tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:129 9dacadc67f274cd7abee5bc5b21415b2
msgid "**Name**: ``OMA_get_protein``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:131 6bc0d20316b34286a0e27978c3ff565c
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get protein information from the OMA (Orthologous "
"MAtrix) Browser by UniProt accession or OMA ID. OMA is a comprehensive "
"orthology database covering 2,600+ complete genomes. Returns protein "
"details including species, genomic location, OMA group membership, and "
"Hierarchical Orthologous Group (HOG) assignment. Example: P04637 returns "
"human TP53 with OMA ID HUMAN31534, HOG:E0739094.3a.3b.3b, and genomic "
"locus on chromosome 17."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/oma_tools.rst:135 e6803af2cf4840f8a606568691017acd
msgid ""
"``protein_id`` (string) (required) UniProt accession (e.g., 'P04637' for "
"human p53) or OMA ID (e.g., 'HUMAN31534'). UniProt accessions are "
"recommended for cross-database compatibility."
msgstr ""

